{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787026545636989001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"brainy-cooked-hog","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"037dbe9469f1644a36b199af58f9ad0b85381168428e5dc10e9f0561b2bbfd2f","event_uuid":"02f17abd-2702-4c64-8a43-55728818f3e5","position":{"commit_sha":"48a0073f580d7fa99e07efd4bc821634d5829eb9","position":"1787022450388966001-02f17abd-2702-4c64-8a43-55728818f3e5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"657b803605fc3c3a712565b0a49a4f5969839cd1d70915d736bebb2a76e845ae","event_uuid":"a8c0ae25-458a-4a66-9586-f5630be8d8ff","position":{"commit_sha":"0af3158d5394cd2230341ebdc072c926b8e333b7","position":"1787022658363864001-a8c0ae25-458a-4a66-9586-f5630be8d8ff"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"7fcf85bae19175768690f5adb9f3175f9daf2322f539ef4c698e5418677761f1","event_uuid":"13797617-4ab7-4f9f-a4d3-791394184eaa","position":{"commit_sha":"9727d44d3c2168210ad81af65b1854610aab306d","position":"1787022900308475001-13797617-4ab7-4f9f-a4d3-791394184eaa"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e97e698edabfe232ef37be71686ac1e770e605dbb4e1a7db791787eef990df0b","event_uuid":"013fdc4d-15c0-40e3-a8b6-435018e038dc","position":{"commit_sha":"66f5fb30b71993344bce65457db0a0a27817f363","position":"1787022994167078001-013fdc4d-15c0-40e3-a8b6-435018e038dc"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787022450388966001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a8c0ae25-458a-4a66-9586-f5630be8d8ff","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"5142-4dbf-9469-4672"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nAfter S1, persistence has a cohesive owner but `BindingStore` still embeds forward/reverse identity transitions, pending/confirmed state, numeric-ID re-key, comment identity, absence grace, tombstones, and unretire policy. Production rich-text convergence also reaches through shallow `all_bindings()` and mutates an inner dictionary, bypassing any future policy seam.\n\n## Outcome\nExtract lifecycle decisions into a private policy owner operating on the repository original dictionaries, with the public facade retaining every existing method/signature. Add a narrow facade operation for rich-text emission state. Preserve shallow `all_bindings()` compatibility, but make the narrow operation the supported production mutation seam for the later caller cutover.\n\n## Plan\n1. Move cohesive forward/reverse, pending/confirmed, immutable-ID re-key, comment-map, absence/retirement, tombstone, suppression, and unretire call clusters into `binding_lifecycle.py`.\n2. Keep the facade authoritative: it coordinates the lifecycle owner and repository unit-of-work; no adapter or reconciler caller receives a writable repository object.\n3. Use open typed views over the same dictionaries. Unknown and legacy fields remain present and writable only through named policy operations.\n4. Add `BindingStore.note_rich_emit(local_id, wire)` (or an equivalently narrow name) that preserves the current counter/hash behavior and missing-binding fail-open result. Do not change `all_bindings()` copy depth.\n5. Preserve exact current failure choices: confirmed 404 grace/reset, moved-key repair, retired corruption fail-open, live corruption fail-closed, append-only comment identity, tombstone suppression, and explicit unretire.\n\n## Testing (RED → GREEN)\n- Direct policy tests exercise both-index transitions and reload through the real repository after each state change.\n- Table-driven tests cover duplicate bind, stale reverse cleanup, missing/corrupt forward state, three-404 retirement, 200 reset, numeric-ID move, legacy no-ID behavior, tombstone suppression/unretire, and changed/unchanged comment IDs.\n- A narrow-operation test compares rich-emission hashes/counters and save behavior to the existing production sequence.\n- Signature and shallow-query regression tests pin the facade compatibility surface.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nFacade delegates can be moved back without changing bytes or callers. This slice adds the narrow mutation operation but does not yet modify RP-04-owned apply files. No lifecycle thresholds, corruption disposition, copy-depth, stored schema, or identity-marker writer changes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Given valid and corrupt forward/reverse combinations, every lifecycle operation preserves at-most-one identity, removes stale reverse entries when required, and safety-aborts ambiguous double binds.\n- [ ] Three confirmed 404s retire, a successful read resets absence, immutable numeric-ID lookup re-keys instead of retiring, and legacy entries retain current behavior.\n- [ ] Tombstoned issues suppress recreate with an alert until explicit unretire; retired corruption and alert-write failures retain their current fail-open boundaries.\n- [ ] Comment IDs remain append-only/change-gated and old records without the field remain readable without rewrite.\n- [ ] The narrow rich-emission operation matches current hash/counter/save behavior while missing bindings remain nonfatal.\n- [ ] Existing facade signatures and shallow `all_bindings()` semantics remain unchanged; no production adapter obtains direct repository mutation access.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_lifecycle.py","reason":"New cohesive identity and lifecycle policy owner."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py","reason":"Retain facade delegates and add the narrow rich-emission operation."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_lifecycle.py","reason":"Direct lifecycle policy and both-index transition tables."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_binding_store_unbind.py","reason":"Corrupt/orphaned reverse cleanup regression coverage."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_binding_store_comment_ids.py","reason":"Append-only comment identity regression coverage."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_binding_move_rekey_heldout.py","reason":"Immutable numeric-ID move and facade signature oracles."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_rich_reemit_state.py","reason":"Narrow rich-emission behavior and compatibility oracle."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","5142-4dbf-9469-4672"],["parent","5e64-d9cd-2dd4-4036"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"5e64-d9cd-2dd4-4036","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["rp02","reconciler","lifecycle","tdd"],"ticket_id":"fc1c-1b08-70c2-4afb","ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-02 S2 — Extract binding lifecycle policy and narrow mutation operations","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_lifecycle.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_binding_store_unbind.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_binding_store_comment_ids.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_binding_move_rekey_heldout.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_rich_reemit_state.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC5","dd_text":"Lifecycle transitions, tombstones, comments, immutable-ID moves, and rich-emission operation"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_store.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_binding_move_rekey_heldout.py","dd_id":"AC6","dd_text":"Facade signatures and shallow binding query compatibility"}]},"source_event_uuids":["02f17abd-2702-4c64-8a43-55728818f3e5","a8c0ae25-458a-4a66-9586-f5630be8d8ff","13797617-4ab7-4f9f-a4d3-791394184eaa","013fdc4d-15c0-40e3-a8b6-435018e038dc"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787026545636989001,"uuid":"872a4318-9c69-42fe-9156-e36742f038d2"}